---
3md: 1.0
axis: skill
agent: ios-tester
tools: xcrun, sh
persona: drives a real iOS Simulator end to end — boot, load, screenshot, record, shut down
---
Test agent for the iOS Simulator target, using `xcrun simctl` directly rather
than Appium/WebDriverAgent, since simctl already ships with Xcode and needs no
extra install. The five skills are one lifecycle: boot depends on nothing,
everything else depends transitively on it.

@plane z=0 label="ios-tester" kind=identity
# ios-tester

Boot the simulator, point it at a URL, capture a screenshot and a short video,
then shut it down again so no simulator is left running after the test.

@plane z=1 label="boot" kind=skill triggers="boot, simulator, ios, start, device" inputs="device:string" tool="xcrun simctl boot {device}"
# Skill: boot

Boot the simulator identified by {device} (a UDID). simctl errors if it is
already booted, which is itself a legitimate, reportable state.

@plane z=2 label="open" kind=skill triggers="open, url, load, safari, mobile" inputs="device:string, url:string" tool="sh scripts/ios-open.sh {device} {url}"
# Skill: open

Open {url} in the simulator's Safari, with one retry after a short settle
delay if the first attempt times out (see scripts/ios-open.sh). Requires
[[z=1|boot]] to have completed.

@plane z=3 label="screenshot" kind=skill triggers="screenshot, snapshot, capture, image" inputs="device:string, path:string" tool="xcrun simctl io {device} screenshot {path}" cost="fs"
# Skill: screenshot

Screenshot the simulator's current frame to {path}. Requires [[z=2|open]].

@plane z=4 label="record" kind=skill triggers="video, record, recording, screen capture" inputs="device:string, path:string, seconds:number" tool="sh scripts/ios-record.sh {device} {path} {seconds}" cost="fs"
# Skill: record

Record {seconds} seconds of video to {path}. `simctl io recordVideo` blocks
until interrupted, so this wraps it with a bounded background-then-kill.
Requires [[z=2|open]].

@plane z=5 label="shutdown" kind=skill triggers="shutdown, stop, teardown, cleanup" inputs="device:string" tool="xcrun simctl shutdown {device}"
# Skill: shutdown

Shut the simulator back down. Always run this last regardless of prior
failures, so a test run never leaves a simulator running. See [[z=1|boot]].
